WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.962
Module 9 expands from individual text and time transformations to broader data-cleaning workflows.

00:00:06.962 --> 00:00:12.707
You will use SQL to identify missing values, standardize inconsistent data, validate rules,

00:00:12.707 --> 00:00:16.372
and address duplicate records.

00:00:16.372 --> 00:00:23.862
The ideas from Module 8 remain important because many cleaning tasks depend on correct text normalization and

00:00:23.862 --> 00:00:26.157
temporal interpretation.

00:00:26.157 --> 00:00:33.747
Before moving on, make sure you can explain what each transformation changes and what meaning it preserves.

00:00:33.747 --> 00:00:38.172
As you move forward, keep the reasoning habits from this module.

00:00:38.172 --> 00:00:43.957
The next topic will add new SQL tools, but it still depends on understanding grain, missing values,

00:00:43.957 --> 00:00:47.386
and the meaning of each transformation.
